    "norm": "Asserts that {@code substitutor} turns {@code template} into {@code expected} through every way {@link StringSubstitutor} can perform substitution: the {@code replace} overloads that return a new value, and the {@code replaceIn} overloads that mutate a buffer in place. <p>Because the template here contains variables, an offset/length substitution that trims the leading and trailing character still yields the full {@code expected} result, since the trimmed characters are plain text and are left untouched.</p>"
